  body: "# Upper Tribunal determination of a forfeiture question\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter says
    that forfeiture rule questions are determined by the Upper Tribunal, after which the case returns to the DM
    to dispose of in light of that decision.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source distinguishes periods before
    and from 25 July 1986 and limits modification, including the murder exclusion in DMG 76006 across PDF pages
    3–4. It also discusses future claims arising from the same killing. These are source statements awaiting legal
    review, not project powers.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 76005, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 76007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 76031, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch76` — PDF SHA-256 `074f2d3f00d4886954d5cbd6ba2653ec407c1ff9f0160a0ca74d337227f9f542`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `53eb7c5ec81ced813ac2faf2af9f772c5f3e9662112a7ef678dcb4daef0b73f8`.\n"
